-- What `==` on a `Dict` answers (`docs/design/static-dispatch-spike.md`
-- §5.3 and §11, amended 2026-10-02; A.74).
--
-- `Dict` is `pub opaque type Dict k v = Dict (Tree k v)`. Until 2026-10-02
-- module `Dict` declared no `pub eq`, so §3.3 fell through to derivation
-- and derived over the SHAPE — the red-black tree, node by node, colour and
-- all — and two dictionaries holding the same pairs were equal only when
-- the insertions happened to build the same tree. This fixture printed that
-- finding: lines three and four were `False` and `True`.
--
-- It builds one dictionary forwards and one backwards from the same four
-- pairs — `fromList` inserts left to right, so the two trees are built in
-- opposite orders; four is the smallest number of keys whose two trees
-- differ — and prints, in order: the two sizes, whether the two
-- dictionaries are `==`, whether their `toList`s are `==`, and whether a
-- dictionary equals itself. Module `Dict` now declares `pub eq`, which
-- compares the pairs in key order, so lines three and four agree.
-- `run/DictSetEquality` covers every spelling and `Set`.
import Dict
import Node exposing (Program)
import String


show : Bool → String
show b =
    if b then
        "True"
    else
        "False"


main : Program
main =
    forwards = Dict.fromList [ ( "a", 1 ), ( "b", 2 ), ( "c", 3 ), ( "d", 4 ) ]
    backwards = Dict.fromList [ ( "d", 4 ), ( "c", 3 ), ( "b", 2 ), ( "a", 1 ) ]
    Node.printLines
        [ String.fromInt (Dict.size forwards)
        , String.fromInt (Dict.size backwards)
        , show (forwards == backwards)
        , show (Dict.toList forwards == Dict.toList backwards)
        , show (forwards == forwards)
        ]
